1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,000
Your washer fluid just froze solid

2
00:00:02,000 --> 00:00:04,000
— and it cracked the reservoir.

3
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:06,500
No spray, just a dry click.

4
00:00:06,500 --> 00:00:09,000
In freezing weather, that's a warning sign, not a fluke.

5
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:12,000
Summer-blend fluid — or plain water —

6
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:15,000
can freeze solid below thirty-two degrees.

7
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:18,000
Frozen fluid expands.

8
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:21,000
That can crack the plastic reservoir, the pump, even the lines.

9
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:23,500
A winter-rated fluid, rated to negative twenty or lower,

10
00:00:23,500 --> 00:00:26,000
can keep that from happening.

11
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:28,000
Worth checking before the first hard freeze.

12
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:30,000
Stop by and we'll take a look — Nick's Tire & Auto.
